AU  - Vázquez-Villa, Cristopher
AU  - Ocharán-Hernández, Jorge Octavio
AU  - Pérez-Arriaga, Juan Carlos
AU  - Hernández-González, Lizbeth A.
T2  - CONISOFT 2025
AB  - Despite their central role in video games, research on design of game mechanics remains understudied and conceptually fragmented. This study reviews the current state of game mechanics design, identifying mechanics, design approaches, tools to assist design and trends. Through a Systematic Literature Review (SLR) of 39 studies published between 2019 and 2024, we identified that core and movement mechanics are regularly addressed, although inconsistencies in their conceptualization. Many design approaches emphasize player experience, but few offer formal frameworks. Design patterns are the dominant approach, while structured methodologies are rarely documented. Unity and MDA were the most cited tools. Only a few studies addressed broader trends, but some pointed to changes in player expectations and mobile development. The design of game mechanics remains an underexplored area in game development research.
