AB  - Game designers have to satisfy the needs of different player types. This paper presents a generalizable concept for switching between different play styles or genres without changing the basic game elements. As an example we employ speciﬁc combinations of parametrized game elements to emulate well-known genres: platformer, shooter, and puzzle games that can be switched at run-time by the player. We discuss ﬁrst insights gained through a preliminary study.
